<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    weather: what being caught out in the rain does to somebody's mood (RimWorld: ThoughtDefOf.SoakingWet,
    reached through WeatherDef.exposedThought — the same route here). Its own file rather than an addition to
    Thoughts_Memories.xml, for the reason CLAUDE.md gives: the loader reads every file under this directory
    and a new file cannot conflict with another lane mid-edit on the shared one.

    A memory rather than a situational thought, as RimWorld's is: a pawn who runs inside is still wet for a
    while. durationDays and baseMoodEffect are RimWorld's shapes recalled, not sourced; the weather tests pin
    that standing out in the rain costs mood and that going inside stops it getting worse, never the numbers.
    WeatherManager.ExposedThoughtIntervalTicks decides how often a pawn still outside renews it, and
    stackLimit 1 means renewing never stacks.
  -->

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>SoakingWet</defName>
    <durationDays>0.25</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>1</stackLimit>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>soaking wet</label>
        <description>I am drenched. Water is running down my back.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-8</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

</Defs>
